From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: microblaze: locate the signal frame from the trampoline

The MicroBlaze signal-frame unwinder (Ramin Moussavi's, gcc 15.3/16.2) locates
the sigcontext with "uc = pc - sizeof (ucontext_t); sc = &uc->uc_mcontext",
using the C library's ucontext_t.  Under glibc that type is much larger than the
kernel's struct ucontext (its uc_sigmask is 128 bytes, the kernel's 8), so the
subtraction overshoots and unwinding through a signal frame fails.

Anchoring on the handler's CFA instead (an earlier fix) works on a stock kernel
but breaks once the kernel reserves an ABI argument-save area at the FRONT of
the rt_sigframe (the MicroBlaze siginfo-clobber fix): that moves &siginfo off
the handler's stack pointer, and no fixed CFA offset serves both kernels.

Anchor on the trampoline, which is the LAST member of the kernel's rt_sigframe,
so the sigcontext is a fixed distance below it regardless of any front reserve;
this is how the arm unwinder copes with its two kernel frame layouts.  Compute
that distance with a local struct that uses the KERNEL sigset_t size, not the C
library's.  Verified under qemu-system-microblazeel (petalogix-s3adsp1800) on a
6.12 kernel built both stock and with the arg-save-reserve patch: _Unwind_Backtrace
from a signal handler recovers the full interrupted chain on both.

	* config/microblaze/linux-unwind.h (microblaze_fallback_frame_state):
	Locate the sigcontext from the rt_sigreturn trampoline using a
	kernel-sized ucontext, instead of the C library's ucontext_t.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/libgcc/config/microblaze/linux-unwind.h b/libgcc/config/microblaze/linux-unwind.h
index b54704a..db2c782 100644
--- a/libgcc/config/microblaze/linux-unwind.h
+++ b/libgcc/config/microblaze/linux-unwind.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
    data appropriately.  See unwind-dw2.c for the structs.  */
 
 #include <signal.h>
-#include <sys/ucontext.h>
+#include <asm/sigcontext.h>
 #include <asm/unistd.h>
 
 #define MD_FALLBACK_FRAME_STATE_FOR microblaze_fallback_frame_state
@@ -48,30 +48,47 @@ microblaze_fallback_frame_state (struct _Unwind_Context *context,
   if ((unsigned long) pc < 4096)
     return _URC_END_OF_STACK;
 
-  /* The kernel writes the signal trampoline onto the stack
-     (struct rt_sigframe.tramp):
+  /* The kernel writes the rt_sigreturn trampoline into the last member of
+     its rt_sigframe:
 
 	addik r12, r0, __NR_rt_sigreturn
 	brki  r14, 0x8
 
-     and sets the saved r15 to the trampoline address minus 8 (the
-     handler returns with "rtsd r15, 8"), so the unwound return
-     address points 8 bytes before the trampoline.  */
-  if (pc[0] == (0x31800000 | __NR_rt_sigreturn) && pc[1] == 0xb9cc0008)
-    ;
-  else if (pc[2] == (0x31800000 | __NR_rt_sigreturn) && pc[3] == 0xb9cc0008)
-    pc += 2;
+     and sets the handler's r15 to the trampoline address minus 8 (the
+     handler returns with "rtsd r15, 8"), so the unwound return address
+     points 8 bytes before the trampoline; find the trampoline itself.  */
+  const unsigned int *tramp;
+  if (pc[2] == (0x31800000 | __NR_rt_sigreturn) && pc[3] == 0xb9cc0008)
+    tramp = pc + 2;
+  else if (pc[0] == (0x31800000 | __NR_rt_sigreturn) && pc[1] == 0xb9cc0008)
+    tramp = pc;
   else
     return _URC_END_OF_STACK;
 
-  /* The trampoline is the last member of the kernel's rt_sigframe and
-     the ucontext sits directly in front of it.  Anchor there rather
-     than at the CFA so the layout of the frame head does not matter
-     (the kernel may insert an ABI argument-home gap at the front).
-     uClibc's ucontext_t matches the kernel's struct ucontext.  */
-  ucontext_t *uc = (ucontext_t *) ((_Unwind_Ptr) pc - sizeof (ucontext_t));
-
-  sc = (struct sigcontext *) &uc->uc_mcontext;
+  /* Anchor on the trampoline, the LAST member of the kernel's rt_sigframe, so
+     the sigcontext is a fixed distance below it regardless of any argument-save
+     area the kernel reserves at the FRONT of the frame (the MicroBlaze
+     signal-frame arg-save fix).  Use the kernel's struct ucontext
+     (asm/ucontext.h): its uc_sigmask is the kernel sigset_t, unlike the C
+     library's larger ucontext_t, so the trampoline offset comes out right.  */
+  struct kernel_ucontext {
+    unsigned long uc_flags;
+    struct kernel_ucontext *uc_link;
+    stack_t uc_stack;
+    struct sigcontext uc_mcontext;
+    /* The KERNEL's sigset_t (_NSIG == 64, two words), not the C library's,
+       which is 16 times larger; getting this size right is what Ramin's
+       original "pc - sizeof (ucontext_t)" got wrong for glibc.  */
+    unsigned long uc_sigmask[64 / (8 * sizeof (unsigned long))];
+  };
+  struct rt_sigframe {
+    siginfo_t info;
+    struct kernel_ucontext uc;
+    unsigned int tramp[2];
+  };
+  struct rt_sigframe *rt = (struct rt_sigframe *)
+    ((_Unwind_Ptr) tramp - __builtin_offsetof (struct rt_sigframe, tramp));
+  sc = (struct sigcontext *) &rt->uc.uc_mcontext;
 
   new_cfa = sc->regs.r1;
   fs->regs.cfa_how = CFA_REG_OFFSET;
